`),incoming_damage:["## Section: Incoming Strike Damage","","Review the top enemy skills by damage dealt to the squad — what hit us and how hard.","Focus on:","- Enemy burst identification: which 2-3 enemy skills did the most damage? This tells us what comp we are losing to — stab-stripping AoE means better pre-bomb positioning; single-target spike means better peel.",'- Damage timing vs our deaths: did the top enemy skills land BEFORE our death cluster (cause) or AFTER (cleanup)? Separate "this skill killed us" from "we were already down and this finished it."',"- Counter-play signal: if one skill type (e.g. meteor shower, mark bombs) dominates, flag it as the thing to interrupt, LoS, or pre-cleanse next raid.","","Write your incoming-damage callout now, following the format constraints."].join(`
`),positioning:["## Section: Squad Positioning (Distance to Tag)","","Review the squad distance-to-tag distribution — how tight or spread the squad was.","Focus on:","- Cohesion breakdown: what is the 80th percentile distance? If most of the squad is within 600 range we are tight enough to bomb. If it is 900+ we are split and will lose the burst trade.","- Distance-at-death correlation: are the players who died the ones who were farthest from tag? That is a direct coaching point — name the pattern.","- Push readiness: if the distance distribution is tight AND we still lost the fight, the problem is not cohesion — it is execution timing or boon state, and the callout should say so to avoid a wrong takeaway.","","Write your positioning callout now, following the format constraints."].join(`
`),push_timing:["## Section: Commander Push Timing","","Review the per-fight analysis of when pushes happened relative to enemy Stability drops and squad boon states.","Focus on:","- Push vs enemy stab drop: did the bomb land when enemy stab was at 0-5 stacks, or did we push into 15+ stacks? Pushing into stab is a wasted bomb — the highest-impact commander decision metric.","- Push vs squad boon state: did we push with our own boons (Quickness, Might, Stab) fresh, or were we pushing dry? A dry push explains a lost trade even if positioning was right.","- Push frequency / tempo: are we over-pushing (every 10-15 seconds without reset) or under-pushing (sitting on cooldowns while the enemy resets)? Tempo mistakes compound across a raid.","","Write your push-timing callout now, following the format constraints."].join(`
`),boon_strips:["## Section: Boon Strip Comparison","","Review the per-player boon strip counts compared side by side.","Focus on:","- Strip volume pre-bomb: were enough strips landing in the 5-10 seconds before our push? Low strip counts in that window mean we pushed into stab — root cause of lost trades.","- Per-player distribution: is one player doing 70% of the strips, or is it spread across 3-4? Over-reliance on one stripper is a single-point-of-failure — if they are focused, we lose all strip pressure.","- Strip timing alignment: are strips landing too early (enemy re-stacks before push) or too late (after the bomb already hit)? Point at the timing gap, not just the raw count.","","Write your boon-strip callout now, following the format constraints."].join(`
